            <ArticleTitle>Ventilation Defect Percent in Helium-3 MRI as a Biomarker of Severe Outcomes in Asthma.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0091-6749(17)31741-4</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jaci.2017.10.016</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ventilation defect percent (VDP) measured in asthmatics with hyperpolarized helium-3 MRI was more strongly associated with ED visits and hospitalizations due to asthma exacerbation than were conventional biomarkers of lung function and inflammation.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>Copyright © 2017. Published by Elsevier Inc.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
